      "content": "Here's the revised memo:\n\nDear Remote Team,\n\nAs we continue to work from home, let's prioritize our well-being by maintaining proper ergonomic workstation setups and taking steps to prevent common issues like wrist and back pain, as well as eye strain. Here are some tips to help you stay comfortable and productive:\n\n**Workstation Setup:**\n\n* Adjust your chair height to ensure your feet are flat on the floor or on a footrest\n* Position your monitor directly in front of you at a comfortable distance (about 20-25 inches)\n* Keep your keyboard and mouse close to your body and within easy reach\n* Use a document holder to keep papers or documents at eye level\n\n**Eye Care:**\n\n* Use good lighting in your workspace, avoiding harsh overhead lighting or screens in low-light environments\n* Position your monitor to reduce glare, or use a screen protector with a matte finish\n* Follow the 20-20-20 rule: every 20 minutes, look away from your screen and focus on something 20 feet away for 20 seconds\n* Consider adjusting the color temperature or brightness of your display to reduce blue light emission, which can contribute to eye strain\n* Take regular breaks to rest your eyes and give them a chance",
